<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE ORG-OVERRIDABLE SETTINGS, in the lawful seed-metadata shape.

  Same pattern as AAO_People_Question, and for the same reasons: configuration deploys with
  the code, is readable without a query against data the running user may not have access to,
  and carries a SHIPPED DEFAULT plus a PER-ORG OVERRIDE in one row. An untouched org silently
  gets the default; a configured org silently gets its own answer; an upgrade never reaches
  across and changes what a customer set.

  Why a type of its own rather than more fields on AAO_Model_Config: that type is the model
  gateway's configuration and is read on the callout path. A toggle governing whether we may
  create a Contact is a different question with a different owner, and putting it there would
  make "is the model active" and "may we write to your CRM" one row to get wrong.

  Owed here at packaging and named rather than assumed: the internal-domain list, which is the
  right value in the wrong home (a demo static resource) per architecture v3.8 item 4.
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <label>AAO Setting</label>
    <pluralLabel>AAO Settings</pluralLabel>
    <visibility>Public</visibility>
</CustomObject>
